# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE suppression list for my-app
#
# Add CVE IDs here (one per line) to suppress specific findings that have been
# reviewed and accepted as non-exploitable in this context.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # short justification; expiry: YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Example:
#   CVE-2024-12345  # only affects the foo feature which we do not use; expiry: 2025-06-01
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   - Always include a justification comment and a review-by date.
#   - Re-evaluate suppressed CVEs on their expiry date — remove stale entries.
#   - Never suppress CRITICAL CVEs without security team sign-off.
#   - Trivy picks up this file automatically when --ignorefile .trivyignore is passed
#     (see the Docker Build & Push stage in Jenkinsfile).
